{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"contour"},{"type":"text","value":" generates level sets from a regular scalar grid. Import it from the\noptional spatial subpath; it is not included in the root or universal barrel."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { contour } from '@tanstack/charts/spatial/contour'\n\nconst mark = contour(wind, {\n  width: 64,\n  height: 60,\n  value: (row) => Math.hypot(row.u, row.v),\n  thresholds: [2, 4, 6, 8, 10],\n  stroke: '#fff',\n  strokeWidth: 0.75,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"function contour<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: ContourOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<never, never, never>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The mark contributes derived color values but no positional domains or\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartPoint"},{"type":"text","value":" interaction candidates."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Number of columns in the row-major grid"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Number of rows in the row-major grid"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, number?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Numeric identity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scalar grid value"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"thresholds"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number | Iterable<number>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sturges"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Approximate level count or exact scalar levels"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"smooth"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interpolate marching-squares crossings"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"color"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<ContourDatum<TDatum>, ChartKey?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Level value"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Derived value sent to the color scale"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fill"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VisualChannel<ContourDatum<TDatum>, string>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resolved color"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contour fill"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stroke"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VisualChannel<ContourDatum<TDatum>, string>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contour stroke"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fillOpacity"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeOpacity"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeWidth"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renderer default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contour presentation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeDasharray"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contour stroke dash pattern"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"opacity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renderer default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whole-contour opacity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Layer-derived"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable mark ID"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkMotionOptions<never>['motion']"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contour enter, update, and exit motion"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":" must be positive integers, and the source length must be\nexactly "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width * height"},{"type":"text","value":". A numeric threshold count must be a positive integer.\nExact thresholds are copied and sorted without mutating the input iterable."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"grid-and-lifecycle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grid and lifecycle"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source values use row-major order. The first "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" values form Cartesian row\nzero at the bottom of the plot; subsequent rows move upward. Null and nonfinite\nvalues remain missing cells in their original grid positions instead of\nshifting later samples."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Marching-squares topology depends only on the source grid, thresholds, and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"smooth"},{"type":"text","value":", so the mark generates it eagerly when the definition is built.\nOrdinary rendering maps the resulting grid coordinates linearly into the final\nplot rectangle and clips them there. Resizing changes that projection without\nre-estimating topology or requiring positional scales."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every rendered "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ContourDatum<TDatum>"},{"type":"text","value":" contains:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":", the scalar threshold;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"source"},{"type":"text","value":", the finite source rows; and"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sourceIndexes"},{"type":"text","value":", their original input indexes."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Presentation accessors receive this derived datum and the complete rendered\ncontour array."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"geometry-and-interaction","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Geometry and interaction"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each level is one structured scene area containing all disconnected polygons\nand holes. SVG, Canvas, React Native SVG, hit geometry, gradients, and clipping\nconsume the same rings; the mark does not author SVG path strings or depend on\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"d3-geo"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A level can contain several disconnected regions, and an aggregate centroid\ncan fall outside all of them. The mark therefore does not manufacture a focus\ntarget or tooltip datum. Layer an interactive source mark only when the grid\nsamples themselves should own focus and tooltips."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"grid-and-lifecycle","text":"Grid and lifecycle","level":2},{"id":"geometry-and-interaction","text":"Geometry and interaction","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`contour` generates level sets from a regular scalar grid. Import it from the\noptional spatial subpath; it is not included in the root or universal barrel.\n\n```ts\nimport { contour } from '@tanstack/charts/spatial/contour'\n\nconst mark = contour(wind, {\n  width: 64,\n  height: 60,\n  value: (row) => Math.hypot(row.u, row.v),\n  thresholds: [2, 4, 6, 8, 10],\n  stroke: '#fff',\n  strokeWidth: 0.75,\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction contour<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: ContourOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<never, never, never>\n```\n\nThe mark contributes derived color values but no positional domains or\n`ChartPoint` interaction candidates.\n\n## Options\n\n| Option                                            | Type                                          | Default          | Meaning                                        |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `width`                                           | `number`                                      | Required         | Number of columns in the row-major grid        |\n| `height`                                          | `number`                                      | Required         | Number of rows in the row-major grid           |\n| `value`                                           | `Channel<TDatum, number?>`                    | Numeric identity | Scalar grid value                              |\n| `thresholds`                                      | `number \\| Iterable<number>`                  | Sturges          | Approximate level count or exact scalar levels |\n| `smooth`                                          | `boolean`                                     | `true`           | Interpolate marching-squares crossings         |\n| `color`                                           | `Channel<ContourDatum<TDatum>, ChartKey?>`    | Level value      | Derived value sent to the color scale          |\n| `fill`                                            | `VisualChannel<ContourDatum<TDatum>, string>` | Resolved color   | Contour fill                                   |\n| `stroke`                                          | `VisualChannel<ContourDatum<TDatum>, string>` | None             | Contour stroke                                 |\n| `fillOpacity`, `strokeOpacity`, and `strokeWidth` | `number`                                      | Renderer default | Contour presentation                           |\n| `strokeDasharray`                                 | `string`                                      | None             | Contour stroke dash pattern                    |\n| `opacity`                                         | `number`                                      | Renderer default | Whole-contour opacity                          |\n| `id`                                              | `string`                                      | Layer-derived    | Stable mark ID                                 |\n| `motion`                                          | `ChartMarkMotionOptions<never>['motion']`     | None             | Contour enter, update, and exit motion         |\n\n`width` and `height` must be positive integers, and the source length must be\nexactly `width * height`. A numeric threshold count must be a positive integer.\nExact thresholds are copied and sorted without mutating the input iterable.\n\n## Grid and lifecycle\n\nSource values use row-major order. The first `width` values form Cartesian row\nzero at the bottom of the plot; subsequent rows move upward. Null and nonfinite\nvalues remain missing cells in their original grid positions instead of\nshifting later samples.\n\nMarching-squares topology depends only on the source grid, thresholds, and\n`smooth`, so the mark generates it eagerly when the definition is built.\nOrdinary rendering maps the resulting grid coordinates linearly into the final\nplot rectangle and clips them there. Resizing changes that projection without\nre-estimating topology or requiring positional scales.\n\nEvery rendered `ContourDatum<TDatum>` contains:\n\n- `value`, the scalar threshold;\n- `source`, the finite source rows; and\n- `sourceIndexes`, their original input indexes.\n\nPresentation accessors receive this derived datum and the complete rendered\ncontour array.\n\n## Geometry and interaction\n\nEach level is one structured scene area containing all disconnected polygons\nand holes. SVG, Canvas, React Native SVG, hit geometry, gradients, and clipping\nconsume the same rings; the mark does not author SVG path strings or depend on\n`d3-geo`.\n\nA level can contain several disconnected regions, and an aggregate centroid\ncan fall outside all of them. The mark therefore does not manufacture a focus\ntarget or tooltip datum. Layer an interactive source mark only when the grid\nsamples themselves should own focus and tooltips.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Contour Mark\ndescription: Reference for regular scalar-grid contours, thresholds, orientation, source lineage, and structured multipolygon output.\n---\n\n`contour` generates level sets from a regular scalar grid. Import it from the\noptional spatial subpath; it is not included in the root or universal barrel.\n\n```ts\nimport { contour } from '@tanstack/charts/spatial/contour'\n\nconst mark = contour(wind, {\n  width: 64,\n  height: 60,\n  value: (row) => Math.hypot(row.u, row.v),\n  thresholds: [2, 4, 6, 8, 10],\n  stroke: '#fff',\n  strokeWidth: 0.75,\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction contour<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: ContourOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<never, never, never>\n```\n\nThe mark contributes derived color values but no positional domains or\n`ChartPoint` interaction candidates.\n\n## Options\n\n| Option                                            | Type                                          | Default          | Meaning                                        |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `width`                                           | `number`                                      | Required         | Number of columns in the row-major grid        |\n| `height`                                          | `number`                                      | Required         | Number of rows in the row-major grid           |\n| `value`                                           | `Channel<TDatum, number?>`                    | Numeric identity | Scalar grid value                              |\n| `thresholds`                                      | `number \\| Iterable<number>`                  | Sturges          | Approximate level count or exact scalar levels |\n| `smooth`                                          | `boolean`                                     | `true`           | Interpolate marching-squares crossings         |\n| `color`                                           | `Channel<ContourDatum<TDatum>, ChartKey?>`    | Level value      | Derived value sent to the color scale          |\n| `fill`                                            | `VisualChannel<ContourDatum<TDatum>, string>` | Resolved color   | Contour fill                                   |\n| `stroke`                                          | `VisualChannel<ContourDatum<TDatum>, string>` | None             | Contour stroke                                 |\n| `fillOpacity`, `strokeOpacity`, and `strokeWidth` | `number`                                      | Renderer default | Contour presentation                           |\n| `strokeDasharray`                                 | `string`                                      | None             | Contour stroke dash pattern                    |\n| `opacity`                                         | `number`                                      | Renderer default | Whole-contour opacity                          |\n| `id`                                              | `string`                                      | Layer-derived    | Stable mark ID                                 |\n| `motion`                                          | `ChartMarkMotionOptions<never>['motion']`     | None             | Contour enter, update, and exit motion         |\n\n`width` and `height` must be positive integers, and the source length must be\nexactly `width * height`. A numeric threshold count must be a positive integer.\nExact thresholds are copied and sorted without mutating the input iterable.\n\n## Grid and lifecycle\n\nSource values use row-major order. The first `width` values form Cartesian row\nzero at the bottom of the plot; subsequent rows move upward. Null and nonfinite\nvalues remain missing cells in their original grid positions instead of\nshifting later samples.\n\nMarching-squares topology depends only on the source grid, thresholds, and\n`smooth`, so the mark generates it eagerly when the definition is built.\nOrdinary rendering maps the resulting grid coordinates linearly into the final\nplot rectangle and clips them there. Resizing changes that projection without\nre-estimating topology or requiring positional scales.\n\nEvery rendered `ContourDatum<TDatum>` contains:\n\n- `value`, the scalar threshold;\n- `source`, the finite source rows; and\n- `sourceIndexes`, their original input indexes.\n\nPresentation accessors receive this derived datum and the complete rendered\ncontour array.\n\n## Geometry and interaction\n\nEach level is one structured scene area containing all disconnected polygons\nand holes. SVG, Canvas, React Native SVG, hit geometry, gradients, and clipping\nconsume the same rings; the mark does not author SVG path strings or depend on\n`d3-geo`.\n\nA level can contain several disconnected regions, and an aggregate centroid\ncan fall outside all of them. The mark therefore does not manufacture a focus\ntarget or tooltip datum. Layer an interactive source mark only when the grid\nsamples themselves should own focus and tooltips.\n"}
